    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Copies answering, by service (HPA scales scoring 2-8)",
      "description": "Pods that answered Prometheus at least once in the last 30 s. One missed read under load (a busy pod answering /metrics late) doesn't count as a pod gone; a removed pod drops out within 30 s. scoring-svc's count rises when its HPA adds copies (docs/results/scaling.md). On compose every service has one copy.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 56,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 0,
          "custom": {
            "axisSoftMax": 8
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count by (app) (max_over_time(up{app=~\"scoring-svc|ingest-svc|alert-svc|kong\"}[30s]) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Mesh: new connections per second, encrypted or not",
      "description": "Connections each pod's Linkerd proxy accepted (docs/mtls.md). mTLS: from another pod in the mesh, encrypted and both ends proven. Not mTLS: Kubernetes' probes from the node, and Kong's public port (clients outside the cluster). Anything else unencrypted is worth a look. Cluster only: compose has no mesh.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 64,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cps",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (app) (rate(tcp_open_total{direction=\"inbound\", tls=\"true\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}} mTLS"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (app) (rate(tcp_open_total{direction=\"inbound\", tls!=\"true\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}} not mTLS"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Mesh: callers refused by policy",
      "description": "Connections or requests a proxy refused because the caller had no mesh identity (the namespace accepts only meshed callers, except Kong's public port). ST3 makes these on purpose; at other times they mean something outside the mesh tried to call a service.",
